  Hi, all. I've tried out the latest driver from D-Link, which they
sent to me after I reported problems this weekend. I keep getting
transmit timeouts, but so far the driver seems to recover OK. I've
appended my kernel logs. The flood of logs is disturbing, and I wonder
if this is supposed to be normal behaviour?

I do note that it always seems to be the same interface (eth1) that is
timing out. Is this perhaps because the link is auto negotiated to
100 Mb/s half duplex, and the other end (which doesn't do auto
negotiation correctly), is set to 100 Mb/s full duplex?

I still haven't had a response to how I'm supposed to force the
interface. My best guess is that I need the following in
/etc/modules.conf:
options sundance media='"autosense,100mbps_fd,autosense"'

but this doesn't seem to make any difference.

				Regards,

					Richard....
